The schema contains nine entity types: an Aircraft identified by icao24; a time-specific Observation identified by icao24 plus time; a Location and AbsolutePoint for each observation; a Velocity for each observation; separate barometric and geometric Altitude entities; and time-specific AlternateIdentifier entities for callsign and squawk. Callsign and squawk justify AlternateIdentifier because the schema explicitly provides multiple identifier schemes, while icao24 remains the stable aircraft subject and source identifier.

Aircraft maps to bsm:Aircraft with high confidence because icao24 explicitly identifies an airframe. Each timestamped row maps to bsm:Observation and connects from the aircraft through bsm:hasObservation. The observation connects to the location, velocity, both altitude measurements, and its callsign and squawk identifier assignments.

The heading column presents a near-synonym issue between bsm:headingAngle and bsm:absoluteBearingAngle. “Heading” alone would suggest headingAngle, but the description explicitly says it is track over ground rather than nose heading; that qualifier selects bsm:absoluteBearingAngle on Velocity, so no Orientation entity is created. vertrate cannot map to bsm:inclinationAngle because vertical speed in metres per second is not an angle. onground is also left unmapped because it is a time-varying boolean, whereas bsm:operatingModeCode is an aircraft-level code and would merge potentially conflicting observations.

Both altitude columns map to bsm:altitudeMeters through distinct Altitude subjects. The ontology has no property that records the barometric-versus-GNSS qualifier, so the distinction is retained only in their distinct subject identifiers and cannot be represented as an ontology property.

Every IRI transformation was checked against its referenced subject transformation: observation_{icao24}_{time}, location_{icao24}_{time}, point_{icao24}_{time}, velocity_{icao24}_{time}, barometric_altitude_{icao24}_{time}, geometric_altitude_{icao24}_{time}, callsign_identifier_{icao24}_{time}, and squawk_identifier_{icao24}_{time} match character-for-character. No unused transformation key is included.

